CVE-2022-25235
CVE-2022-25236

# Accepted upstream-owned findings — real CVEs in Python dependencies
# resolved by the Hermes installer (mcp 1.26.0, python-multipart 0.0.27,
# starlette 1.0.1). Not patched here: the uv environment is upstream's
# tested set, and this image tracks upstream as closely as possible; the
# fix arrives with a Hermes release. Exposure: MCP/ASGI server-side
# components, and the only server run is the Hermes backend (`hermes
# serve`, spawned by the desktop app on an ephemeral 127.0.0.1 port, or
# the opt-in dashboard on 127.0.0.1:9119) behind the password-gated VNC
# display — "no known remote path", not "proven unreachable".
# Re-evaluate on every HERMES_VERSION bump.
CVE-2026-52869
CVE-2026-52870
CVE-2026-59950
CVE-2026-53539
CVE-2026-48818
CVE-2026-54283

# Same regime as the entries above, all in the Python environment the
# Hermes installer resolves (uv.lock) or in the CPython build uv ships:
#
# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 — msgpack 1.1.2 out-of-bounds read, fixed in
#   1.2.1. Only ever decodes payloads the agent produced in the pod.
# CVE-2026-97687 / CVE-2026-97689 — urllib3 2.7.0 (HTTPS-proxy TLS
#   override, chunk-parser DoS), fixed in 2.8.0. No proxy is configured
#   in the image, and the agent's HTTP traffic is its own outbound calls.
# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools 70.3.0 path traversal in PackageIndex,
#   fixed in 78.1.1. It sits in uv's own CPython distribution, not in
#   hermes' venv, and nothing installs packages at runtime: the tree is
#   root-owned and the pod rootfs is read-only.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
CVE-2025-47273

# Same regime again, re-evaluated for HERMES_VERSION v2026.9.24:
#
# CVE-2026-102266/102267/102268/102271/102272/102273 — PyJWT 2.13.0
#   (key confusion, JWKS redirect, BOM forgery), fixed in 2.14.0. A
#   direct upstream pin (pyproject.toml, already annotated with its
#   PYSEC ids). Hermes does decode bearer JWTs server-side (dashboard
#   OAuth verifier in plugins/dashboard_auth, the chronos cron-fire
#   webhook on the serve/dashboard and gateway listeners, a no-op that
#   never reaches jwt.decode until cron.chronos.expected_audience and
#   nas_jwks_url are configured (none here)), but every verifying call
#   pins `algorithms=` to asymmetric algs (the only unverified decodes
#   are diagnostics after a failed verify and a client-side read of the
#   agent's own API key), the dashboard providers register only once an
#   operator configures an IdP (none here), and the servers bind
#   127.0.0.1 behind the VNC display.
# CVE-2026-111064 / GHSA-2g87-pp6c-29x5 — aiohttp 3.14.3 (DoS), fixed
#   in 3.14.4. Pulled by the `[all]` extras; its servers (platform
#   webhooks, the gateway API server) start only with platform
#   credentials / an API_SERVER_KEY the image ships none of, and the pod
#   exposes nothing but VNC.
# CVE-2026-63374 — anyio 4.12.1 (TLS cert spoofing via IDN encoding),
#   fixed in 4.14.2. Async backend of the agent's outbound HTTP clients
#   only; needs an on-path attacker on an IDN host the agent reaches.
# CVE-2026-84381 / CVE-2026-84382 — httpcore2/httpx2 2.7.0 (SOCKS5
#   WebSocket plaintext, decompression amplification), fixed in
#   2.10.0/2.12.0. The MCP SDK's outbound client; it honours
#   HTTP(S)_PROXY/ALL_PROXY (socks:// included), but the image sets no
#   proxy, so the SOCKS path is never taken.
CVE-2026-102266
CVE-2026-102267
CVE-2026-102268
CVE-2026-102271
CVE-2026-102272
CVE-2026-102273
CVE-2026-111064
GHSA-2g87-pp6c-29x5
CVE-2026-63374
CVE-2026-84381
CVE-2026-84382
